Most hack abuses I know of can only be really useful to a character
that is already pretty advanced.  Here is the single most powerful
abuse I know of; powerful because (1) it can get you almost any item
in the game, and (2) it is useful to all but the weakest characters.
This method will therefore often make the difference between getting
to the point of polypiling, and dying on level 9 or 10.

It's a pretty ugly spoiler, thus:



Don't you hate being teased by more than one ^L ?



OK, you are resolved to win, but can't seem to get the right things.
The key idea is to *put* the right things where you can find them, via
ghost (bones) levels.  

First, a little info on ghost levels.  Any time you die on level 4 or
deeper, there is a 1/3 chance that you will write a bones file.
Anybody playing hack later will have a 1/3 chance of hitting that
level when they come to it.  The item about bones levels to remember
is that *only* the items the character actually has in their inventory
when they die may be cursed in the bones file.  (And in fact, they are
quite like to be cursed if so... I seem to recall the number is 80%.)

Thus, take a character (which I will call a porter, for obvious
reasons) down to level 4 -- and die intentionally, which may (1/3
chance) create a ghost file.  Drop all your worthwhile items before
dying.  Repeat until you actually create a ghost file, which you can
check by looking in the right place -- the System folder on Macs, 
/usr/local/games/lib/nethackdir/ on the local unix installation, you
will have to do a little searching.  Bones files will be named
"bones_04" or "bones_09" etc.

Do the same for levels 5, 6, 7...  however many you feel you need.
Actually, its better to decide beforehand how many ghost levels you
are going to create, then create the lowest ones first.  This way you
do not run into your own ghost levels taking more porters down to
leave another one.

Now you take the character you actually want to win with down.  If you
have scattered ghost files across even two levels, 4 and 5, there is a
pretty good (5/9) chance of getting at least one.  Which means, you
are rich.  You can have more than twice as much loot as is normal for
an average game at that level.  Furthermore, by choosing the porter
correctly, you can leave yourself most anything.  Wizard porters can
start the game with blindfolds, magic markers, rings of T and P
control or conflict, wands of death or polymorph...  Valkyries always
get a +3 shield and a +1 longsword, which translates into Excaliber
quickly enough.  Use other porters to taste.

If you can, make sure to kill your porters on altar levels -- this
insures you an altar in whatever game hits that bones!  (For the
*really* choosy, make sure the altar is lawful, and you will have
insured yourself holy water.)  Similarly, arranging a bones on a shop
level is also a worthwhile idea.  Another way to slightly improve the
scam is to actually search downward further levels beyond the one
which you are targetting to die on.  This increases the amount of
stuff you can find even more.  It is generally a good idea to always
mark levels you intend to ghost somehow -- I used to always pile my
stuff near the up stairs, so it will be found immediately.  Also, lock
your dog in a room if you can, or dump it higher up if you do not
think you will want it later.  You can even write in the dust beneath
specific items if you know what they are.

Finally, remember: any time you *know* you are going to die, and have
no hope, type 'D' then 'a'.  This will prevent all of your uncursed
items except armor from being cursed, in the event that bones are
written.

